  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "40223060",
      "title": "Effective POM",
      "lectureOrder": 117,
      "videoOrder": 116,
      "sourceHash": "a563de81947bf8b9a42f111c991d2e102935f327e06919bee129e4d887b1a6d6",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.002,
          "end": 2.88,
          "en": "(gentle piano music)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.88,
          "end": 4.38,
          "en": "-: So till this point we have talked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.38,
          "end": 5.46,
          "en": "about the POM file, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 5.46,
          "end": 7.47,
          "en": "Which is P-O-M.XML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 7.47,
          "end": 9.69,
          "en": "Now, in this you can mention different stuff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 9.69,
          "end": 11.91,
          "en": "Of course, to configure your Maven",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 11.91,
          "end": 15.15,
          "en": "you have to make changes in this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 15.15,
          "end": 17.25,
          "en": "Now, if you want to create a package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 17.25,
          "end": 18.93,
          "en": "we have to mention certain things, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 18.93,
          "end": 21.66,
          "en": "So for your own project, if you want to make a JAR file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 21.66,
          "end": 25.29,
          "en": "you basically need the groupId, you need artifactId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 25.29,
          "end": 26.73,
          "en": "you need a version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 26.73,
          "end": 28.8,
          "en": "So that's how you can create a JAR file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 28.8,
          "end": 31.44,
          "en": "Or maybe you can create your own libraries, if you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 31.44,
          "end": 34.32,
          "en": "And then in your project, if you want some dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 34.32,
          "end": 36.27,
          "en": "you have to mention those dependencies here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 36.27,
          "end": 38.76,
          "en": "So we have a dependency stack in which you can mention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 38.76,
          "end": 40.2,
          "en": "multiple dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 40.2,
          "end": 42.57,
          "en": "And it's not limited to one or two dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 42.57,
          "end": 46.02,
          "en": "We can create as many dependencies as you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 46.02,
          "end": 48.54,
          "en": "or you can have as many dependencies you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 48.54,
          "end": 50.79,
          "en": "In fact, when you work with Spring framework,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 50.79,
          "end": 52.83,
          "en": "you have to add the Spring dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 52.83,
          "end": 54.36,
          "en": "If you are working with Lombok,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 54.36,
          "end": 56.73,
          "en": "you have to add Lombok dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 56.73,
          "end": 58.11,
          "en": "So it's not limited, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 58.11,
          "end": 60.75,
          "en": "So basically you can mention everything here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 60.75,
          "end": 62.67,
          "en": "And then this dependency can depend upon some other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 62.67,
          "end": 64.44,
          "en": "dependencies, which we have talked about before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 64.44,
          "end": 66.18,
          "en": "which are your transitive dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 66.18,
          "end": 69.72,
          "en": "Apart from this, what if you want to work with some plugins?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 69.72,
          "end": 73.56,
          "en": "Of course you can add an extract tag here for the plugins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 73.56,
          "end": 74.78999999999999,
          "en": "And even that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 74.78999999999999,
          "end": 77.49,
          "en": "So you can see, you can add a plugins repository",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 77.49,
          "end": 78.66,
          "en": "where we can mention those things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 78.66,
          "end": 81.24,
          "en": "And you can configure the way you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 81.24,
          "end": 83.31,
          "en": "how you want it to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 83.31,
          "end": 85.89,
          "en": "But apart from this, of course even if you don't mention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 85.89,
          "end": 88.17,
          "en": "any plugin, but you're still able to do those things, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 88.17,
          "end": 91.5,
          "en": "So what is happening is the pom.xml, by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 91.5,
          "end": 94.86,
          "en": "it will show you certain things which you want to change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 94.86,
          "end": 96.78,
          "en": "but there are more settings to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 96.78,
          "end": 99.3,
          "en": "which is not even visible to you, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 99.3,
          "end": 101.37,
          "en": "So this is not the effective POM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 101.37,
          "end": 103.02000000000001,
          "en": "So there's a concept called effective POM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 103.02000000000001,
          "end": 107.91,
          "en": "also called a super POM, which is the parent, you can say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 110.49000000000001,
          "en": "So basically whatever changes you make here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 110.49000000000001,
          "end": 112.86,
          "en": "is also reflected in the effective POM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 112.86,
          "end": 115.86,
          "en": "So let's say when Maven wants to work with your project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 115.86,
          "end": 117.78,
          "en": "they will not look at the POM file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 117.78,
          "end": 120,
          "en": "And I know, 'till this point you're talking about POM file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 120,
          "end": 123.21,
          "en": "but they'll look at something called effective POM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 123.21,
          "end": 125.7,
          "en": "It will have the configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 125.7,
          "end": 128.07,
          "en": "as well as the configuration in which you have done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 128.07,
          "end": 129.84,
          "en": "But how will you see that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 129.84,
          "end": 132.78,
          "en": "So, different IDEs have a different way of showing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 132.78,
          "end": 134.37,
          "en": "In fact, I started working on Maven",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 134.37,
          "end": 139.11,
          "en": "using NetBeans ID way back, and it was having a tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 139.11,
          "end": 140.67000000000002,
          "en": "extra tab for effective POM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 140.67000000000002,
          "end": 142.35,
          "en": "We are using IntelliJ here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 142.35,
          "end": 143.57999999999998,
          "en": "So again, once we...",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 143.57999999999998,
          "end": 145.59,
          "en": "I will also show you a demo of Eclipse",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 145.59,
          "end": 146.79,
          "en": "in which we'll try to find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 146.79,
          "end": 148.23,
          "en": "how do you get the effective POM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 148.23,
          "end": 151.53,
          "en": "But here, if you, you're working with IntelliJ,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 151.53,
          "end": 153.81,
          "en": "what you do is just right-click on your pom.xml.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 153.81,
          "end": 156.99,
          "en": "And if you go down, you will see this option of Maven.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 156.99,
          "end": 161.13,
          "en": "And if you go here, there's option of Show Effective POM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 161.13,
          "end": 164.22,
          "en": "When you click on this, it will look like a POM file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 164.22,
          "end": 165.42000000000002,
          "en": "but the name is different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 165.42000000000002,
          "end": 167.91,
          "en": "And if you see, there are more things to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 167.91,
          "end": 169.29,
          "en": "than what you have added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 169.29,
          "end": 170.55,
          "en": "Of course there's a dependency,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 170.55,
          "end": 171.96,
          "en": "but if you go down there's something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 171.96,
          "end": 174.45,
          "en": "called pluginPepository, and that's where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 174.45,
          "end": 176.94,
          "en": "you are getting all the plugins by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 176.94,
          "end": 178.35,
          "en": "even if you have not added them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 178.35,
          "end": 180.35,
          "en": "There are resources as well. Plugins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 180.35,
          "end": 182.82,
          "en": "So you can see we have all this plugin to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 182.82,
          "end": 184.08,
          "en": "So there's a plugin for autorun,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 184.08,
          "end": 187.02,
          "en": "there's a plugin for clean, there's a plugin for resources,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 187.02,
          "end": 189.99,
          "en": "there's a plugin for JAR for the package which you do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 189.99,
          "end": 191.49,
          "en": "There's a plugin for compiler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 191.49,
          "end": 193.29,
          "en": "So everything is there by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 193.29,
          "end": 196.53,
          "en": "Even if you don't mention that in the POM file, it's there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 196.53,
          "end": 198.54,
          "en": "So there basically there's a effective POM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 198.54,
          "end": 201.93,
          "en": "which is getting created for every Maven project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 201.93,
          "end": 203.49,
          "en": "So whatever changes you make,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 203.49,
          "end": 205.35,
          "en": "don't make changes in the effective POM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 205.35,
          "end": 208.62,
          "en": "You as a developer make changes in the pom.xml.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 208.62,
          "end": 211.05,
          "en": "So it'll create its effective POM here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 211.05,
          "end": 212.52,
          "en": "So this is called effective POM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 212.52,
          "end": 214.77,
          "en": "or you can say super POM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 214.77,
          "end": 216.393,
          "en": "Different names, but same thing.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
